    "created_at": "2019-05-12T23:23:50Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-05-12T23:23:50Z",
    "body": "Thanks for taking the time to comment @Hixie!\r\n\r\nI'm only too keen for this discussion to reach a terminus of any kind. However, the actual question was: **is there a reason** the non-standard word \"seeked\" was used? \r\n\r\n* That \"seeked\" is non-standard I hope isn't up for debate (the entry in your folk dictionary confirms this)\r\n* That language and its so-called standards are subject to change isn't in question either\r\n* The subject of inquiry is **why** this non-standard word was used, and (by implication) what process or discussion preceded its inclusion\r\n\r\nMy assumption is that there was/is no process or discussion.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
